# PicoPiAndPortable — busybox config fragment
# Applied on top of allnoconfig via build_busybox.sh
#
# Single busybox binary built only for the few applets PPAP hasn't
# replaced natively yet (sed today).  The default /bin/sh is PPAP's
# own push shell.
#
# Key design choices:
#   - NOMMU mode (no fork, vfork-only)
#   - PIE linking with musl libc (R_ARM_RELATIVE relocations for XIP)
#   - Coreutils + editors + filesystem + shell
#   - No Linux-specific features (sendfile, utmp, syslog)

# -- Platform -----------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_STATIC is NOT set — we use -pie to get .rel.dyn relocations.
# The exec.c loader needs these to fix up function-pointer arrays
# (e.g. applet_main[]) whose entries are raw link-time addresses.
CONFIG_NOMMU=y

# -- Size optimization --------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_LFS=y

# -- File operations ----------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_LS is not set (using native PPAP ls)
# CONFIG_CAT is not set (using native PPAP cat)
# CONFIG_CP is not set (using native PPAP cp)
# CONFIG_MV is not set (using native PPAP mv)
# CONFIG_RM is not set (using native PPAP rm)
# CONFIG_MKDIR is not set (using native PPAP mkdir)
# CONFIG_RMDIR is not set (using native PPAP rmdir)
# CONFIG_LN is not set (using native PPAP ln; hard-link only, no -s)
# CONFIG_CHMOD is not set (using native PPAP chmod)

# -- Text processing ----------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_ECHO is not set (push built-in)
# CONFIG_PRINTF is not set (using native PPAP printf)
# CONFIG_GREP is not set (using native PPAP grep)
# CONFIG_HEAD is not set (using native PPAP head)
# CONFIG_TAIL is not set (using native PPAP tail; stdin not yet supported)
# CONFIG_WC is not set (using native PPAP wc)
# CONFIG_SORT is not set (using native PPAP sort)
# CONFIG_SED is not set (using native PPAP sed)

# -- Process management -------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KILL is not set (using native PPAP kill)
# CONFIG_SLEEP is not set (using native PPAP sleep)
# CONFIG_PS is not set (using native PPAP ps)
# CONFIG_TOP is not set (using native PPAP top)
# CONFIG_FEATURE_TOP_INTERACTIVE is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_TOP_CPU_USAGE_PERCENTAGE is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_TOP_CPU_GLOBAL_PERCENTS is not set

# -- Filesystem utilities -----------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_MOUNT is not set (using native PPAP mount)
# CONFIG_UMOUNT is not set (using native PPAP umount)
# CONFIG_DF is not set (using native PPAP df)

# -- Editor -------------------------------------------------------------------
# vi disabled — replaced by pi (PiPAPo Editor)
# CONFIG_VI is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_VI_COLON is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_VI_SEARCH is not set

# -- System -------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_UNAME is not set (using native PPAP uname)

# -- Shell --------------------------------------------------------------------
# hush dropped — PPAP's `push` is /bin/sh.  No system script needed bash
# compatibility, and shipping two shells doubled the binary footprint.
# CONFIG_HUSH is not set
# CONFIG_SH_IS_HUSH is not set

